## =============================================================================
## .github/workflows/release.yml.template — build, scan and publish the image
## =============================================================================
## GUIDE STEP   12.2 (release and deploy with Compose: the platform image and
##              the Caddy image, since compose.yml has Caddy from 9.0)
## PURPOSE      On every merge to `main`:
##                1. build the platform image once (Dockerfile.platform);
##                2. tag it with the git commit SHA (unique, never reused);
##                3. scan it with Trivy (stop on HIGH/CRITICAL);
##                4. push it to GitHub Container Registry (GHCR) as
##                   ghcr.io/soweluavanzo/te-verifier:<sha>;
##                5. the same for the Caddy image (deploy/caddy/Dockerfile)
##                   as ghcr.io/soweluavanzo/te-verifier-caddy:<sha>
##                   (compose.prod.yml runs it from the first deploy).
##              The server then deploys that exact tag (docs/operations.md):
##              it never builds code itself.
## WHY THE .template SUFFIX
##              Same reason as ci.yml.template: a fully commented file in
##              .github/workflows/ is reported as invalid. Activate by
##              uncommenting and renaming to release.yml.
## USED BY      GitHub Actions; compose.prod.yml pulls the pushed images.
## DEPENDS ON   Dockerfile.platform, deploy/caddy/Dockerfile (9.0);
##              repository setting "Workflow permissions" allowing
##              packages: write (see `permissions` below).
## WHY          Architecture D13 / guide 12.2: what runs in production is
##              exactly the image that passed CI, identified by its commit;
##              rollback = deploy the previous SHA.
## ACTIVATE     Uncomment the 12.2 code, rename, merge to main, then check the
##              package under github.com/SoweluAvanzo?tab=packages. Make the
##              package private or public deliberately (GHCR packages start
##              private; the server must be able to pull it; the same for
##              te-verifier-caddy). Lint first:
##                docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/repo" -w /repo rhysd/actionlint:1.7.12
##              Actions are pinned to commit SHAs (see ci.yml.template).
