## Guide 12.2
## [ ] 1. `name: Release image`, triggered only by a push to main.
## [ ] 2. `permissions`: contents: read and packages: write (nothing else).
## [ ] 3. `jobs:` → `release` on ubuntu-latest, with a job-level env
##        IMAGE: ghcr.io/soweluavanzo/te-verifier.
## [ ] 4. Steps: checkout, then docker/login-action to ghcr.io with
##        github.actor and the run's secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN (both actions
##        pinned to a commit SHA, as in ci.yml.template).
## [ ] 5. Build once, tagged with the full commit SHA:
##          | - run: docker build -f Dockerfile.platform \
##          |     -t "$IMAGE:${{ github.sha }}" .
## [ ] 6. Trivy scan of that image BEFORE pushing (same settings as the
##        `image` job of ci.yml.template), then `docker push` of the tag.
## [ ] 7. The Caddy image (compose.yml has Caddy since 9.0, so production
##        needs it from the first deploy): in the env, CADDY_IMAGE:
##        ghcr.io/soweluavanzo/te-verifier-caddy; then build deploy/caddy
##        with the same tag, scan it with the same Trivy settings, push it:
##          | - run: docker build -t "$CADDY_IMAGE:${{ github.sha }}" \
##          |     deploy/caddy
## [ ] 8. Last step: write "Deploy with TE_IMAGE_TAG=<sha>" into
##        $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY.
## [ ] 9. Check: merge to main, see the run pass, and find both packages,
##        with the same tag, under github.com/SoweluAvanzo?tab=packages; set
##        their visibility on purpose.
